Package: dockplane-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Dockplane <info@dockplane.de>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Dockplanee/dockplane
Depends: adduser, systemd
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Dockplane agent for a managed Docker host
 Connects one Docker host to a Dockplane control server. It reports host
 facts, container state and Compose projects, streams a container's output,
 and starts, stops or restarts a container the control server asks it to.
 .
 The set of operations is fixed at build time. There is no remove, exec,
 attach or shell, and no request from the control server carries a command
 to run on the host.
 .
 The agent holds its own certificate, obtained once by enrolling with a
 short-lived token, and connects outward: nothing needs to reach into the
 managed host. This package installs no identity and enables no service.
 .
 The agent needs access to the Docker socket, which is equivalent to root
 on this host. See /usr/share/doc/dockplane-agent/README.Debian.
